      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "Why does the milkman add a very small amount of baking soda to fresh milk? &#2342;&#2370;&#2343;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2340; &#2325;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Why does the milkman add a very small amount of baking soda to fresh milk?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2342;&#2370;&#2343;&#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2361;&#2369;&#2340; &#2325;&#2350; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "To reduce the pH of the fresh milk from 6 to slightly more acidic &#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330; 6 &#2360;&#2375; &#2341;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">To reduce the pH of the fresh milk from 6 to slightly more acidic</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330; 6 &#2360;&#2375; &#2341;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "To increase the pH of the fresh milk from 6 to slightly alkaline &#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330; 6 &#2360;&#2375; &#2341;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">To increase the pH of the fresh milk from 6 to slightly alkaline</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330; 6 &#2360;&#2375; &#2341;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "To maintain the pH of the fresh milk at 6 for a longer time &#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; 6 &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2352;&#2326;&#2344;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">To maintain the pH of the fresh milk at 6 for a longer time</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; 6 &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2319; &#2352;&#2326;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "To reduce the pH of the fresh milk from 6 to slightly alkaline &#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330; 6 &#2360;&#2375; &#2341;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">To reduce the pH of the fresh milk from 6 to slightly alkaline</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2332;&#2375; &#2342;&#2370;&#2343; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330; 6 &#2360;&#2375; &#2341;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>&#183; Fresh milk is slightly acidic (pH ~6).</p><p>&#183; Adding baking soda (NaHCO&#8323;) makes it slightly alkaline, preventing it from turning sour quickly due to lactic acid formation.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "Chemical formula of washing soda is ______. &#2343;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2366; (&#2357;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2366;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2370;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; ______ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Chemical formula of washing soda is ______.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2343;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2366; (&#2357;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2366;) &#2325;&#2366; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2370;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; ______ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Na 2 CO 3 .10H 2 O Na 2 CO 3 .10H 2 O",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Na<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>.10H<sub>2</sub>O</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Na<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>.10H<sub>2</sub>O</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Na 2 SO 4 Na 2 SO 4",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Na<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">Na<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub></span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "NaOH NaOH",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">NaOH</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">NaOH</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "NaHCO 3 NaHCO 3",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">NaHCO<sub>3</sub></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">NaHCO<sub>3</sub></span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>Washing soda, also known as sodium carbonate decahydrate, has the chemical formula <b>Na<sub>2</sub>CO<sub>3</sub>&#183;10H<sub>2</sub>O</b>. It is an inorganic compound that consists of sodium (Na), carbon (C), oxygen (O), and water (H2O) molecules. The presence of ten water molecules in its structure makes it a hydrate.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "Select the synthetic indicator from among the given options. &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2367;&#2306;&#2341;&#2375;&#2335;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Select the synthetic indicator from among the given options.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2367;&#2306;&#2341;&#2375;&#2335;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Turmeric &#2361;&#2354;&#2381;&#2342;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Turmeric</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2354;&#2381;&#2342;&#2368;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Cabbage juice &#2327;&#2379;&#2349;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2352;&#2360;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Cabbage juice</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2379;&#2349;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2352;&#2360;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Litmus solution &#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2350;&#2360; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Litmus solution</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2350;&#2360; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Methyl orange &#2350;&#2367;&#2341;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Methyl orange</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2367;&#2341;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>&#183; <b>Methyl orange</b> is a <b>synthetic indicator</b>, meaning it is artificially prepared in laboratories. It is commonly used in acid-base titrations.</p><p>&#183; It turns <b>red in acidic</b> solutions and <b>yellow in basic</b> solutions.</p><p><b>Further Insight:</b></p><p>&#183; <b>Turmeric</b>  -  Natural indicator (from the turmeric plant).</p><p>&#183; <b>Cabbage juice</b>  -  Natural indicator (from red cabbage).</p><p>&#183; <b>Litmus solution</b>  -  Derived from lichens, so it's a <b>natural indicator</b>.</p>",
