      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Which of the following is the compound with the chemical formula H&#8322;SO&#8324;? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2351;&#2380;&#2327;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2370;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; H&#8322;SO&#8324; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is the compound with the chemical formula H&#8322;SO&#8324;?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2351;&#2380;&#2327;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2370;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; H&#8322;SO&#8324; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Nitric Acid &#2344;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2319;&#2360;&#2367;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Nitric Acid</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2319;&#2360;&#2367;&#2337;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Sulfuric Acid &#2360;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2319;&#2360;&#2367;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Sulfuric Acid</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2319;&#2360;&#2367;&#2337;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Sulfurous Acid &#2360;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2352;&#2360; &#2319;&#2360;&#2367;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Sulfurous Acid</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2352;&#2360; &#2319;&#2360;&#2367;&#2337;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Hydrogen Sulfide &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2360;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Hydrogen Sulfide</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2360;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>&#183; <b>H&#8322;SO&#8324;:</b> The chemical formula for <b>Sulfuric Acid</b>, a strong mineral acid with the structure H&#8322;SO&#8324; (two hydrogens, one sulfur, four oxygens).</p><p>&#183; <b>Other Options:</b></p><p>o <b>Nitric Acid:</b> HNO&#8323;, used in fertilizers and explosives.</p><p>o <b>Sulfurous Acid:</b> H&#8322;SO&#8323;, a weaker acid formed from sulfur dioxide.</p><p>o <b>Hydrogen Sulfide:</b> H&#8322;S, a toxic gas, not an acid in this context.</p><p><b>Further Insights:</b></p><p>&#183; <b>Industrial Uses:</b> Sulfuric acid is a \"king of chemicals,\" used in batteries, fertilizers (e.g., ammonium sulfate), and chemical synthesis.</p><p>&#183; <b>Properties:</b> Highly corrosive, it dehydrates substances and is a strong dehydrating agent (e.g., chars sugar).</p><p>&#183; <b>Safety:</b> Handling H&#8322;SO&#8324; requires precautions due to its reactivity, a key topic in chemistry education.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "What are bases that are soluble in water called? &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2328;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2358;&#2368;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2361;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What are bases that are soluble in water called?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2328;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2358;&#2368;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2361;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Alkenes &#2319;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Alkenes</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2354;&#2381;&#2325;&#2368;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Acids &#2319;&#2360;&#2367;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Acids</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2360;&#2367;&#2337;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Alkalis &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Alkalis</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Alkanes &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Alkanes</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2344;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Bases that are soluble in water are called <b>Alkalis</b>. When dissolved in water, alkalis produce hydroxide ions (OH&#8315;). All alkalis are bases, but not all bases are alkalis (some bases are insoluble in water).</p><p><b>Explanation of Other Options:</b></p><p>&#8226; Alkenes: These are unsaturated hydrocarbons containing at least one carbon-carbon double bond. They are organic compounds, not related to the definition of water-soluble bases.</p><p>&#8226; Acids: Acids are substances that produce hydrogen ions (H&#8314;) or hydronium ions (H&#8323;O&#8314;) when dissolved in water, or are proton donors. They are the chemical opposites of bases.</p><p>&#8226; Alkanes: These are saturated hydrocarbons consisting only of hydrogen and carbon atoms and all bonds are single bonds. They are organic compounds.</p><p><b>Further insights:</b></p><p>&#8226; Examples of alkalis include sodium hydroxide (NaOH), potassium hydroxide (KOH), and calcium hydroxide (Ca(OH)&#8322; - sparingly soluble).</p><p>&#8226; Alkalis typically have a bitter taste and feel soapy to the touch (due to saponification of fats on the skin).</p><p>&#8226; They turn red litmus paper blue and react with acids to form salt and water (neutralization).</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "Acid changes the colour of blue litmus to _________ &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2344;&#2368;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2350;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; _________ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Acid changes the colour of blue litmus to _________</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2344;&#2368;&#2354;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2335;&#2350;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; _________ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Yellow &#2346;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Yellow</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Red &#2354;&#2366;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Red</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2366;&#2354;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Pink &#2327;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366;&#2348;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Pink</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366;&#2348;&#2368;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Orange &#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Orange</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>Acid turns blue litmus <b>red</b>. Bases turn red litmus blue.</p><p>Special type of substances are used to test whether a substance is acidic or basic. These substances are known as indicators. The indicators change their colour when added to a solution containing an acidic or a basic substance. Turmeric, litmus, china rose petals (Gudhal), etc., are some of the naturally occurring indicators.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "Which substance is commonly used as an acid-base indicator, which turns red in acidic solutions and blue in basic solutions? &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2346;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2340;&#2307; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;-&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2351; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which substance is commonly used as an acid-base indicator, which turns red in acidic solutions and blue in basic solutions?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2346;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2340;&#2307; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;-&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2351; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2366;&#2354; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;&#2351; &#2357;&#2367;&#2354;&#2351;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
