      "solution": "<p>&bull; Litmus paper is commonly used acid-base indicator, which turns red in acidic solution and blue in basic solution</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Indicator</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Original Color</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">In Acid</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">In Base</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Red Litmus Paper</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Red</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">No change</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Turns blue</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Blue Litmus Paper</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Blue</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Turns red</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">No change</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Phenolphthalein</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Colorless</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Colorless</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Pink</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Methyl Orange</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Orange</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Red</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Yellow</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Turmeric</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Yellow</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"bor