      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "Which theory, independently introduced in 1923, led to the concept of acid-base conjugate pairs? 1923 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;-&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2332;&#2344;&#2381;&#2350; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which theory, independently introduced in 1923, led to the concept of acid-base conjugate pairs?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>1923 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;-&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2351;&#2369;&#2327;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2357;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2332;&#2344;&#2381;&#2350; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Lewis's theory &#2354;&#2369;&#2312;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Lewis's theory</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2369;&#2312;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Br&#248;nsted-Lowry theory &#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2375;&#2337;-&#2354;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Br&#248;nsted-Lowry theory</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2348;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2375;&#2337;-&#2354;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Arrhenius theory &#2309;&#2352;&#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2360; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Arrhenius theory</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2352;&#2361;&#2375;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2360; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Davy's theory &#2337;&#2375;&#2357;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Davy's theory</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2337;&#2375;&#2357;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p>&bull; A Br&#248;nsted-Lowry acid is a substance that can donate a proton (H&#8314;), and a Br&#248;nsted-Lowry base is a substance that can accept a proton</p><p>&bull; A Lewis acid is a substance that can accept an electron pair, while a Lewis base is a substance that can donate an electron pair.</p><p>&bull; An Arrhenius acid is a substance that increases the concentration of hydrogen ions (H&#8314;) in aqueous solution, while an Arrhenius base increases the concentration of hydroxide ions (OH&#8315;).&#8203;</p><p>&bull; Sir Humphry Davy proposed that acids are substances that contain replaceable hydrogen atoms, and their acidic properties are due to the presence of hydrogen.&#8203;</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5e061e27cfa8-q9",
      "number": 9,
      "question": "Acidic drain cleaners made of ______ or ______ acid are powerful enough to clear heavy-duty hair, food, grease, soap scum or paper-based clogs in 15 minutes or less. ______ &#2351;&#2366; ______ &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2351; &#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2325; (&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2344;&#2352;) 15 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2351;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;-&#2349;&#2352;&#2325;&#2350; &#2348;&#2366;&#2354;, &#2349;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;, &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2360;, &#2360;&#2366;&#2348;&#2369;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354; &#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2327;&#2332;-&#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2357;&#2352;&#2379;&#2343; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2347; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2358;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Acidic drain cleaners made of ______ or ______ acid are powerful enough to clear heavy-duty hair, food, grease, soap scum or paper-based clogs in 15 minutes or less.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>______ &#2351;&#2366; ______ &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2350;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2351; &#2344;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2325; (&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2368;&#2344;&#2352;) 15 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2351;&#2366; &#2313;&#2360;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;-&#2349;&#2352;&#2325;&#2350; &#2348;&#2366;&#2354;, &#2349;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;, &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368;&#2360;, &#2360;&#2366;&#2348;&#2369;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354; &#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366;&#2327;&#2332;-&#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2357;&#2352;&#2379;&#2343; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2347; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2358;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "formic, citric &#2347;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">formic, citric</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "nitric, carbonic &#2344;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2379;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">nitric, carbonic</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2379;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "sulphuric, hydrochloric &#2360;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2379;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">sulphuric, hydrochloric</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2379;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "malic, lactic &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2354;&#2376;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2367;&#2325;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">malic, lactic</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;, &#2354;&#2376;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2367;&#2325;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>Acidic drain openers are made with <b>hydrochloric or sulfuric acids</b>. This type of drain opener is best for grease clogs, heavy-duty hair build-up, organic waste, soap scum, or tough clogs in a shower or kitchen sink. Their effectiveness to dissolve clogs is almost unmatched due to their chemical makeup. They are best used on newer pipes in a home or commercial setting, as the strength of this cleaner may damage older pipes. Users should wear protective gear while using this opener.</p>",
